Per axum@0.8.9:

Construct with `Router::new()` (default state type `S = ()`). Build it via the builder: `Router::new().route("/", get(handler))` and optionally `.with_state(s)` / `.nest(...)` / `.layer(...)` — see `Router<S = ()>` in src/routing/mod.rs. To serve it, pass the `Router` directly to `axum::serve(listener, router).await` (the serve doc shows `let router = Router::new().route("/", get(|| async { "Hello, World!" })); ... axum::serve(listener, router).await.unwrap();`). The `Router::into_make_service` signature is `pub fn into_make_service(self) -> IntoMakeService<Self>` (plus `pub fn into_make_service_with_connect_info<C>(self) -> IntoMakeServiceWithConnectInfo<Self, C>`), and `impl<S> IntoMakeService<S> {}` is defined in src/routing/into_make_service.rs.

